{{define "header"}}Basic Parser

Queries are designed to process, filter, and summarize data effectively.
Specifically, queries allow you to:
- Filter out irrelevant data
- Select specific components of the data to view
- Group, summarize, and calculate metrics on the data

You can construct queries progressively. Here are examples of how to build them:{{end}}

{{define "sortIntro"}}	Explanation: This sorts the resulting data based on the specified fields.
	You can specify the sort direction with `asc` (ascending, default) or `desc` (descending).
	Example: `sort c.Category asc c.Amount desc`
	Missing values (nil) are ordered before strings (i.e. empty string semantics).
	You can also limit the number of rows output by appending `limit N` (e.g. `limit 10`).{{end}}

